								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=269"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="http://www.ascentguild.com" title="Ascent Guild" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/www_sm.gif" alt="WWW" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:Ssnakess@mail2hell.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=537.msg4155#msg4155"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=537.msg4155#msg4155">Re:Gnos</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #18 on:</b> December 29, 2003, 05:26:25 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							You do realize that the guild management tool can see through /role, right?<br /><br />I mean, I do have friends in your guild who could check for me...<br /><br />The brother bit is rather funny...you know...my dad can beat up your dad.<br /><br />About this gaining and losing members constantly, I bet you haven&#039;t done a lot of research on that comment, or you wouldn&#039;t have said it. &nbsp;Sure there are periods of mass growth, and some losses here and there....but they are the same for most other guilds. &nbsp;You can say you have known the members of your guild for 4-5 years, and I am sure we have members who have known each other that long as well.<br /><br />I personally haven&#039;t been on this server for 4 years, so that is kind of hard for me to pull off~<br /><br />And finally...<br /><br />Despite your belief, and I say your belief because I am sure everyone else isn&#039;t dumb enough to believe it, those of us in &quot;uber guilds&quot; do realize the difference in the players of &quot;uber guilds&quot; and &quot;casual guilds&quot;. &nbsp;It&#039;s not rocket science, you have people who play all the time, and people who don&#039;t. &nbsp;You also have people who want to spend the majority of their game time advancing their character, and people who want to spend most of their time having fun. &nbsp;Let&#039;s face it, raiding isn&#039;t always fun.<br /><br />Now let me tell you something you obviously don&#039;t know. &nbsp;Us &quot;uber guilds&quot; have just as much fun, and are probably closer to a few (not all of course) of the other members of our guilds than a &quot;casual guild&quot; player could ever be. &nbsp;The reason? &nbsp;Because while &quot;casual guild&quot; players don&#039;t tend to log in as much as &quot;uber guild&quot; players (it&#039;s not always true of course, there are always exceptions to the rule) the &quot;uber guild&quot; players are nearly always around one another, and when you grind and raid with someone nearly every day, it is very easy to develope a bond with that person.<br /><br />Oh and one more thing. &nbsp;You do realize that they do bans, soulmarks, and suspensions on the entire account...not the char...and that they can check what account the char belongs to, so if you create a new char..its just like training with your main...right? &nbsp;You aren&#039;t really so gullible as to think that you could simply create a new character and get away with anything you wanted...are you?
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
